! Documents

Here are some educational documents, listed in ascending order of complexity.

# ((What Is Lojban?, The Book|What Is Lojban?)), an introductory book covering a wide range of basic information on the Lojban language.
#  Robin Turner and Nick Nicholas's [http://ptolemy.tlg.uci.edu/~opoudjis/lojbanbrochure/lessons/book1.html|Lojban For Beginners] lessons.
#  [http://www.lojban.org/publications/brochures/lojex.txt|“Diagrammed Summary of Lojban Grammar Forms with Example Sentences”]

After these, see ((Lojban For Advanced Students)).

For vocabulary, you can browse [http://www.lojban.org/jbovlaste/|jbovlaste,] a Lojban dictionary system.

There is also a [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-download_wiki_attachment.php?attId=89|PDF of the first 19 pages of the Level 0 booklet.]

! Forums

You can [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/|join the Lojban beginners' e-mail list] and other ((Lojbanic Forums)).

! Software tools

There is a Lojban-to-English translator at [http://www.lojban.org/jboski/].

You could also try ((Parallel 2)), a program for ((implicit learning)) of Lojban (and other languages). Modules developed for ((Parallel 2)) are strongly influenced by ((What Is Lojban?, The Book|What Is Lojban?)).

Other ((Lojbanic Software)).